{
  "notes": "Ambient, B dorian, 84 BPM in half time. A broadcast heard from very far: ghostly 'ooh' voices whose vowel flickers on a sample-and-hold LFO (VOICE SOUL OOH), a faint beacon that pings a chord tone every two bars into a long dark echo (LOFI on a soft triangle), the player's Wurlitzer on the Smart Keys (minor pentatonic from B3, tremolo, tape-dark echoes), DUST on the master for the hiss and crackle, and glitch ticks for percussion. Scenes: A one chord, the voices in a hollow fifth under the beacon (the beacon alone at low ENERGY); B the dorian vamp (i7, IV add9) two bars each, full voices and the first ticks; C the signal clears and the harmony opens out through III, IV, VII and home; D the signal is lost again, VII sus2 to i add9, four bars each, in a bigger and darker room. All material is original.",
  "format": "flowstate-world/1",
  "id": "lost_signal",
  "name": "LOST SIGNAL",
  "category": "AMBIENT",
  "blurb": "Far voices, dying beacon",
